<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="person-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="person-title">The person behind AccountOrbit</h2>
      <p>I own AccountOrbit and run its day-to-day operations. I handle enquiries and speak with customers myself, so the person you talk to on the first call is the person coordinating your requirement.</p>
      <p class="para">Most people who call know they need accounting or tax help, but aren't yet sure what kind, or who is allowed to provide it. The starting point is usually a GST deadline, a notice, or books that have fallen behind. My job is to turn that into a clear description of the work and the next steps.</p>
      <p class="para">I oversee the communication with you throughout, and coordinate the work as it is agreed with you.</p>
      <p class="para">My personal profiles: {% ext site.owner.facebook, "Facebook" %} and {% ext site.owner.instagram, "Instagram" %}. These are personal accounts, not AccountOrbit company pages.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>What this page does not claim</h2>
      <p>I haven't listed qualifications, career history, memberships or awards on this page, because none has been confirmed for publication.</p>
      <p class="para">Nothing here presents me as a Chartered Accountant, tax adviser, auditor or other regulated practitioner. Work the law reserves for a qualified professional must be done and signed by someone who holds that qualification. For the business itself, see <a href="/about-us/">About AccountOrbit</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="work-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 id="work-title">How I work with you</h2>
      <p>From the first call, you deal with me. This is how an enquiry usually moves, and what you can do to make it quicker.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="deliver-grid">
      <article><h3>When you call</h3><p>I take the call myself. Tell me the task, your type of business and any date you are working to. If a deadline is very close, say so first.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Understanding the requirement</h3><p>We go through what the work involves: the task, the records, the timing, and whether any part is reserved by law for a particular qualification.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Coordinating the next steps</h3><p>I coordinate what happens next and keep you informed. If another professional is needed for part of the work, your details are shared with them only if you agree.</p></article>
      <article><h3>What to have ready</h3><p>What you need done, your type of business, your part of Delhi, and whether it is one-time or recurring. Never share an OTP or portal password, with me or anyone else.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="section-foot">Before any work starts, ask for the scope, the full fee and who will do and sign each part, in writing. See <a href="/how-it-works/">how it works</a> for each stage.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 id="approach-title">My approach to clear information</h2>
      <p>Accounting and tax decisions are easier when the information is plain and you can check it yourself. These are the three rules AccountOrbit's pages follow.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="deliver-grid">
      <article><h3>Separate the kinds of work</h3><p>Bookkeeping, a tax return and a statutory audit are different jobs. Pages explain what a service involves, and which parts the law reserves for particular professionals.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Show where facts come from</h3><p>Tax and legal pages cite official sources such as the GST, Income Tax and Udyam portals, and say when they were checked, so you can confirm the rules yourself.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Publish only what is verified</h3><p>You won't find invented reviews, client counts or credentials here, including mine. If something cannot be confirmed, it is not claimed.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="ask-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 id="ask-title">Questions I recommend asking before choosing a professional</h2>
      <p>Before you agree to accounting or tax-related work, I recommend asking a few straightforward questions. They tell you who will handle the task, what is included and what you need to provide. They apply whoever you speak to, with or without AccountOrbit.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="deliver-grid">
      <article><h3>What work do I need help with?</h3><p>Write down the job first: monthly books, a GST return, an income tax return, a notice reply or an audit. Each needs different skills. See <a href="/services/">services</a>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Which professional is eligible to perform it?</h3><p>Some work is limited by law. A company's statutory audit, for example, must be done by a Chartered Accountant. See <a href="/guides/accountant-vs-chartered-accountant/">accountant vs Chartered Accountant</a>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Who will actually handle the work?</h3><p>The person you meet may not be the person preparing your accounts or returns, so ask who will.</p></article>
      <article><h3>What services are included in the scope?</h3><p>Ask what is included and what is not, in writing, before you agree. Ask, too, how extra work such as a notice reply would be charged.</p></article>
      <article><h3>How are fees and extra costs explained?</h3><p>Ask for the total, with GST and government charges shown. See <a href="/guides/accounting-services-cost-in-delhi/">accounting services cost in Delhi</a>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>What documents will I need?</h3><p>Knowing this early avoids delays close to a deadline. See the <a href="/guides/monthly-accounting-documents-checklist/">monthly documents checklist</a>.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="section-foot">For a fuller walk-through, read <a href="/guides/how-to-hire-an-accountant-in-delhi/">how to hire an accountant in Delhi</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

